# Trivy ignore file — ONE scoped, justified exception. Never a blanket suppression.
#
# History: this file previously ignored ~17 base-image CRITICALs (chromium, libgnutls30,
# loader-utils, shell-quote, tar, Go stdlib). As of the HR-12 change those are now actually
# REMEDIATED in the Dockerfile instead of ignored:
#   • chromium* + libgnutls30  → apt-get --only-upgrade to the fixed Debian 12 releases
#   • GitPython + PyJWT        → pip --upgrade in BOTH the frappe venv and the base /usr/local python
#   • esbuild (Go stdlib CVEs), loader-utils, shell-quote, launch-editor
#                              → deleted (build-only node_modules; not in the runtime path; the
#                                esbuild binary is even arm64 and can't run on this amd64 image)
#
# The single remaining exception cannot be fixed in our layer:
#
# CVE-2026-59873 — node-tar 7.5.1 (gzip-bomb DoS) bundled INSIDE the npm CLI
#   (/home/frappe/.nvm/.../lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/tar).
#   • npm is a build/CLI-time tool, NEVER in ERPNext's request/runtime path → the DoS is not
#     reachable in production (it would require running `npm` against a crafted archive).
#   • The fix (an npm release bundling tar >= 7.5.19) needs node >= 24.15; frappe/erpnext:v16.28.0
#     ships node 24.12, so `npm install -g npm@latest` fails EBADENGINE.
#   • Revisit on the next ERPNext base bump (newer base → newer node+npm → clears on its own).
CVE-2026-59873
